{"name":"Breath of Fire","hex":"#ee0011","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or process of breathing.","A single act of breathing in or out; a breathing of air."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["voiceless, surd; contrasting with voice (breath sounds, voice sounds)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breath"},{"term":"fire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (usually self-sustaining) chemical reaction involving the bonding of oxygen with carbon or other fuel, with the production of heat and the presence of flame or smouldering.","An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and maintained in a specific location to a useful end (such as a campfire or a hearth fire)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Amazing; excellent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breath of Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Breath of Fire is a role-playing video game series developed by Capcom. It originated on the Super Nintendo Entertainment System in 1993. The series has recurring characters and ambiguous continuity; though each game is its own self-contained story, the names of the two lead characters are usually Ryu and Nina."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c5/Breath_of_Fire_logo.png/330px-Breath_of_Fire_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breath_of_Fire"},{"title":"Breath of Fire (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Breath of Fire is a role-playing video game developed by Capcom originally for the Super Nintendo Entertainment System. Initially released in Japan in April 1993, the game was later made available in North America in August 1994 by Square Soft, who handled the title's English localization and promotion. It is the first entry in the Breath of Fire series."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/39/Breath_of_Fire_cover_art.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breath_of_Fire_(video_game)"},{"title":"Breathing","blocks":[{"text":"Breathing is the rhythmic process of inhaling air into the lungs providing oxygen, and exhaling the air removing carbon dioxide, in the gas exchange process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Real-time_MRI_-_Thorax.ogv/330px--Real-time_MRI_-_Thorax.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breathing"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/BOF1battle.PNG/330px-BOF1battle.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/BOF1battle.PNG/330px-BOF1battle.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A battle in Breath of Fire, showing Ryu transformed into a dragon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABOF1battle.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Breath_of_Fire_characters.jpg/330px-Breath_of_Fire_characters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/20/Breath_of_Fire_characters.jpg/330px-Breath_of_Fire_characters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The playable characters of Breath of Fire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreath_of_Fire_characters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg/500px-Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg/1280px-Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg/500px-Ribcage_during_inhalation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibcage_during_inhalation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Costillas_%28gray%29.png/330px-Costillas_%28gray%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Costillas_%28gray%29.png/330px-Costillas_%28gray%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACostillas_(gray).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Quiet_breathing.jpg/500px-Quiet_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Quiet_breathing.jpg/1280px-Quiet_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Quiet_breathing.jpg/500px-Quiet_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuiet_breathing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Forceful_breathing.jpg/500px-Forceful_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Forceful_breathing.jpg/1280px-Forceful_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Forceful_breathing.jpg/500px-Forceful_breathing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AForceful_breathing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Nose_in_cold_weather.gif/500px-Nose_in_cold_weather.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Nose_in_cold_weather.gif/1280px-Nose_in_cold_weather.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Nose_in_cold_weather.gif/500px-Nose_in_cold_weather.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inhaled air is warmed and moistened by the wet, warm nasal mucosa, which consequently cools and dries. When warm, wet air from the lungs is breathed out through the nose, the cold hygroscopic mucus in the cool and dry nose re-captures some of the warmth and moisture from that exhaled air. In very cold weather the re-captured water may cause a \"dripping nose\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANose_in_cold_weather.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Illu_quiz_lung05.jpg/250px-Illu_quiz_lung05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_